# Swallows in the proof pipeline that were read and found unable to weaken a
# verdict. Enforced in both directions by scripts/check-proof-swallow.sh: an
# unlisted swallow fails, and so does a row nothing matches.
#
# One row per (file, enclosing function, pattern occurrence), with the reason above it.
# A row is not an exemption. It is a claim that this particular swallow cannot
# turn an unproven program into a reported-proven one. If that claim is wrong,
# the fix is the code, not the row.
#
# The list only ratchets down. Adding a row is a deliberate widening and should
# carry its reason in the commit as well as here.

# The failure is already reported, and reported the same way whether or not
# this line runs: `self.api_schemas_dynamic = true` on the caller's side marks
# the schema unanalyzable, and null from here is how a non-literal schema
# argument is spelled in the first place. A parse failure and a non-literal
# argument are the same fact to every consumer.
packages/zts/src/contract_builder.zig extractSchemaJson catch-return

# `ensureHealthy` is the checker's poison check, not an error being dropped:
# the pool has already recorded a failure, and returning early stops work that
# would read corrupt types. The poison is surfaced by pipeline.zig, which calls
# `TypeChecker.ensureHealthy` and propagates, so a build cannot finish green on
# a poisoned pool. The binding-map writes and `collectSchemaCompileCall` on the
# same paths call markAllocationFailure, which ensureHealthy also reports.
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig inferType catch-return
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig walkExpr catch-return
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig walkStmt catch-return

# The three narrowing-guard extractors partition a union's members onto the
# heap, and they run on `*const TypeChecker`, so an allocation failure has no
# sticky flag to set. Returning null installs no narrowing, and a binding that
# is not narrowed keeps its declared type - which is wider, never narrower.
# Every check downstream therefore sees more of the type than the guard proved,
# so the failure can add a diagnostic and can never remove one. It cannot turn
# an unproven program into a reported-proven one.
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig resolveAbsentBinding catch-return
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig extractTypeofGuard catch-return
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig extractIsArrayGuard catch-return
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig extractIsDictGuard catch-return
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig extractIsBytesGuard catch-return

# --- Consumer-side acceptance kernel ---
#
# markDeclared marks the nodes a certificate DECLARES total rather than proves.
# A `continue` past an obligation it could not read leaves that node unmarked,
# and an unmarked node is one the consumer's own totality fold must settle for
# itself. The failure therefore costs the producer a declaration it wanted and
# can never grant one it did not earn.
packages/proof-checker/src/checker.zig markDeclared catch-continue

# The `catch return` rejects an artifact that exhausts the budget. This
# function returns `?Rejection`, and a non-null value refuses the artifact.
packages/proof-checker/src/checker.zig bindExecutableGraph catch-return

# The graph-root loop above these searches has already read every member and
# rejected a failed read. A failed read here cannot bypass that binding.
packages/proof-checker/src/checker.zig checkGraphMemberDigest catch-break

# Null means "no certificate-owned members", and this value only ever
# populates the OBSERVED graph the kernel decides against. Omitting a member
# makes the observed root disagree with the root the certificate states, which
# is a rejection; and `accept` hands the same raw certificate bytes to
# `pcc.check`, which decodes them independently and refuses at the decode stage
# if they are undecodable. Neither path can buy acceptance with a null.
packages/runtime/src/proof_activation.zig certificateCommitments catch-return

# The retired-authority check propagates OutOfMemory. Every other contract
# parse error returns InvalidContractSection and stops activation before the
# kernel runs. No failed parse can produce an acceptance verdict.
packages/runtime/src/proof_activation.zig retiredInputFeature catch-switch

# Kernel catch blocks return a Rejection. Neither policy, certificate, guard,
# nor graph decode failure can reach the acceptance result.
packages/proof-checker/src/checker.zig bindExecutableGraph catch-block
packages/proof-checker/src/checker.zig check catch-block
packages/proof-checker/src/checker.zig checkGuardCoverage catch-block

# A missing observed root refuses server startup. Accept converts graph errors
# to refusals; OutOfMemory still propagates.
packages/runtime/src/proof_activation.zig observedRoot catch-switch
packages/runtime/src/proof_activation.zig observedRoot catch-value
packages/runtime/src/proof_activation.zig accept catch-switch

# Invalid extracted endpoints become dynamic, which removes static egress
# proof. Provider and tool fetch failures record a refusal or dynamic reach.
# A schema compilation error either propagates OOM or refuses the tool scope.
# getOrPutDuped releases its new key and propagates the allocation error.
# Query parameter decode failures mark the extraction dynamic.
packages/zts/src/contract_builder.zig normalizeEndpoint catch-value
packages/zts/src/contract_builder.zig getOrPutDuped catch-block
packages/zts/src/contract_builder.zig appendQueryParamsFromSchema catch-block

# Map insertion failure releases its new key and propagates the allocation error.
packages/zts/src/fault_coverage.zig getOrPutEntry catch-block

# HandlerVerifier checks allocation_failed before it returns a verdict. Its
# fact, import, walk, checked-flag journal, shared-alias, and diagnostic catches only defer
# that failure.
packages/zts/src/handler_verifier.zig addDiagnostic catch-poison
packages/zts/src/handler_verifier.zig collectImportBindings catch-poison
packages/zts/src/handler_verifier.zig recordSharedAlias catch-poison
packages/zts/src/handler_verifier.zig resolveFacts catch-block
packages/zts/src/handler_verifier.zig scanImports catch-poison
packages/zts/src/handler_verifier.zig setCheckedFlag catch-poison
packages/zts/src/handler_verifier.zig walkForResultsAndRefs catch-poison

# A nonliteral or incomplete assertion makes the whole intent dynamic. Other
# parse errors propagate; the catch never installs a partial assertion.
packages/zts/src/intent_extractor.zig collectAssertions catch-switch

# TypeChecker and its TypeEnv report allocation poison through ensureHealthy
# before a build can use the inferred types. Local unknown/null values below
# are temporary results while the poisoned checker unwinds.
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig addDiagnostic catch-block
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig admitOneTypePredicate catch-poison
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig bindCallableMetadata catch-block
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig bindForOfElement catch-poison
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig bindPatternBindings catch-poison
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig bindVarDeclaration catch-poison
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig endNarrowScope catch-poison
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig inferObjectLiteralType catch-block
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig putNarrowed catch-poison
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig recordContextType catch-poison
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig recordNarrowChange catch-poison
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig registerParamTypes catch-poison
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig schemaValueToType catch-block
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig schemaValueToType catch-poison
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig walkExpr catch-poison
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig walkStmt catch-poison

# Invalid schema JSON yields no compiled type entry, so no schema shape can be
# inferred from it. Contract extraction independently marks that surface
# dynamic. OutOfMemory still propagates and poisons the checker.
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig schemaJsonToType catch-switch

# Coverage analysis of a `match` allocates only scratch memory and the text of a
# witness. When it cannot, the checker is poisoned (`ensureHealthy` fails the
# pipeline before any result is used) and the match is reported as not
# exhaustive with no redundancy verdict, which is the conservative answer: it
# adds a diagnostic and a `| undefined` to the type and removes nothing.
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig matchCoverage catch-block
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig reportMatchCoverage catch-block

# These catches change only the text of an error diagnostic. The same kind,
# error severity, source node, and error count are recorded.
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig addArgCountMismatch catch-value
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig addArgTypeMismatch catch-value
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig addGenericDiagnostic catch-value
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig addNominalConstructorCall catch-block
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig addReadonlyMutation catch-block
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig addTypeMismatch catch-block
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig checkModuleEncodableArgs catch-value
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig reportIfNonContractive catch-block
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig reportIfUnencodable catch-value

# TypeEnv.ensureHealthy and TypePool.ensureHealthy reject their recorded
# allocation failure before their types can support a verdict.
packages/zts/src/type_env.zig findNonContractiveAliases catch-poison
packages/zts/src/type_env.zig instantiateCompositeMembers catch-block
packages/zts/src/type_env.zig internName catch-block
packages/zts/src/type_env.zig pushGenericScope catch-poison
packages/zts/src/type_env.zig putTypeAlias catch-poison
packages/zts/src/type_env.zig registerCapsuleAlias catch-poison

# This parts function is a test fixture with runtime safety enabled.
# Its fixed member array satisfies computeRoot; no production path calls it.
packages/proof-checker/src/checker.zig parts catch-trap

# Each additional kernel catch in these functions returns a rejection.
packages/proof-checker/src/checker.zig bindExecutableGraph catch-block@2
packages/proof-checker/src/checker.zig bindExecutableGraph catch-block@3
packages/proof-checker/src/checker.zig bindExecutableGraph catch-block@4
packages/proof-checker/src/checker.zig bindExecutableGraph catch-return@2
packages/proof-checker/src/checker.zig check catch-block@2
packages/proof-checker/src/checker.zig check catch-block@3
packages/proof-checker/src/checker.zig check catch-block@4

# Each certificate digest failure returns null to a caller that
# refuses an unreadable graph root or decodes the bytes independently.
packages/runtime/src/proof_activation.zig certificateCommitments catch-return@2
packages/runtime/src/proof_activation.zig certificateCommitments catch-return@3

# A second query parameter decode failure also marks the extraction dynamic.
# The policy hash is hex text produced by the registry from 32 digest bytes;
# decoding into exactly 32 bytes cannot return an invalid-length error.
packages/zts/src/contract_builder.zig appendQueryParamsFromSchema catch-block@2
packages/zts/src/contract_builder.zig currentPolicyHashRaw catch-trap

# The extra verifier catches record poison; verify checks it before it returns.
packages/zts/src/handler_verifier.zig scanImports catch-poison@2
packages/zts/src/handler_verifier.zig walkForResultsAndRefs catch-poison@2
packages/zts/src/handler_verifier.zig walkForResultsAndRefs catch-poison@3

# Each second narrowing allocation failure returns null. The un-narrowed type
# is wider, so these sites cannot remove a required diagnostic.
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig extractIsArrayGuard catch-return@2
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig extractIsBytesGuard catch-return@2
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig extractIsDictGuard catch-return@2
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig extractTypeofGuard catch-return@2

# These extra type-checker catches retain diagnostic kind or set the poison
# that ensureHealthy checks before the result can support a build.
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig inferObjectLiteralType catch-block@2
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig registerParamTypes catch-poison@2
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig schemaValueToType catch-block@2

# TypeEnv and its pool reject poison before a caller can use partial semantic
# types. The numbered rows cover separate insertions in the same function.
packages/zts/src/type_env.zig findNonContractiveAliases catch-poison@2
packages/zts/src/type_env.zig internName catch-block@2

# --- Path generator: decides fault_covered and paths_exhaustive ---
#
# Both walkPaths catches free the loop bound and then `return err`. The error
# propagates to the caller, so no path set is published for that walk.
packages/zts/src/path_generator.zig walkPaths catch-block
packages/zts/src/path_generator.zig walkPaths catch-block@2

# Loop descriptions are display text on a bound whose kind is already chosen.
# An allocation failure shortens the text to a fixed string or to empty, and
# freeLoopBound skips an empty description. The symbolic or unknown kind is
# unchanged, so the summarized walk still blocks exhaustiveness.
packages/zts/src/path_generator.zig allocLoopDesc catch-multiline
packages/zts/src/path_generator.zig allocLoopDesc catch-value

# These three catches only shorten the human-readable test name. The name is a
# label on the generated case. It does not enter the constraints, the stubs,
# or any property the generator reports.
packages/zts/src/path_generator.zig emitTestCase catch-value
packages/zts/src/path_generator.zig emitTestCase catch-value@2

# A failed argument signature leaves the stub without one. Canonicalization
# merges two I/O calls only when both carry a matching non-null signature, so a
# null signature removes a merge and can never add one.
packages/zts/src/path_generator.zig emitTestCase catch-value@3

# A schema that does not parse yields no static item bound. The caller then
# falls through to a symbolic loop bound, which marks the walk as a summary.
# A missing bound cannot become a constant bound.
packages/zts/src/path_generator.zig schemaFieldMaxItems catch-return

# A LIMIT digit run that does not fit in u32 yields no bound. The caller falls
# through to the same symbolic loop bound as for a missing LIMIT clause.
packages/zts/src/path_generator.zig trailingLimitValue catch-value

# --- Pipeline ---
#
# The cleanup block frees the export effects that the failed list append did
# not take, and then returns the error. The multi-module extraction fails.
packages/zts/src/pipeline.zig extractMultiModuleContractWithEntry catch-block

# Failure to build effect facts is cached as `.unavailable`. The path generator
# reads `.unavailable` as "reaches recursion", and that blocks fault_covered.
# The failure moves the result toward unproven.
packages/zts/src/pipeline.zig pathEffectFacts catch-block

# The output is 20 bytes: a four-digit year, five two-digit fields, and fixed
# punctuation. The buffer holds 24 bytes, so bufPrint cannot overflow.
packages/zts/src/pipeline.zig formatIsoTimestamp catch-trap

# --- Proof IR lowering ---
#
# The collector stores the first error in `failed`, skips all later children,
# and the caller returns `failed` after the walk. The lowering fails as a whole.
packages/zts/src/proof_ir.zig visit catch-block
packages/zts/src/proof_ir.zig visit catch-block@2

# --- Translation witness recorder ---
#
# Every catch sets `incomplete`. Recorder.check returns WitnessIncomplete when
# that flag is set, and a recording that is not whole yields no certificate.
packages/zts/src/translation_witness.zig applyCompaction catch-block
packages/zts/src/translation_witness.zig notePreOptimizationLen catch-block
packages/zts/src/translation_witness.zig recordRewrite catch-block
packages/zts/src/translation_witness.zig recordRewrite catch-block@2

# --- Imported-file analysis for CHECK (precompile_imports.zig) ---
#
# The imported flow traversal and the imported fault scan decide what an
# imported file contributes to the handler's flow, effect, and fault verdicts.
# Both traversals answer in one direction: every failure to reach an answer is
# a blocked effect, an incomplete module graph, or a blocked fault entry.
#
# Extensionless paths reach this call after `std.fs.path.extension` found no
# extension. `file_resolver.resolve` fails only with OutOfMemory, which
# propagates here, or with UnsupportedSourceExtension, which needs an extension
# on the path. The unreachable arm is a claimed invariant, not an error result:
# if the claim failed, the build would trap and no verdict would be reported.
packages/tools/src/precompile_imports.zig resolveCheckImportPath catch-switch

# `graph.load` fails with OutOfMemory, which propagates, or with an unreadable
# or unparsable imported file. The other errors set `graph.complete = false`
# and return the default analysis: a `.blocked` effect and no flow target.
# A blocked effect merges as the top row (every capability, impure, writes,
# egress, lower bound) into the importer. `complete = false` makes the flow
# evaluator record `module_graph_gap`, and any unresolved construct clears
# every flow property. Neither result is cleaner than a successful load.
packages/tools/src/precompile_imports.zig analyzeImportedFunction catch-switch

# The three type-check catches set `type_check_clean = false`. That choice sets
# `graph.complete = false` (flow properties clear), skips `finishModule` and
# the flow target, and blocks every relative import of the file in the effect
# inputs. The effect analysis then runs with `type_source = .omitted`. The type
# environment is read at one place in effect_inference.zig, the function
# `contributeDeclaredCallbackRow`, which returns false without it. The caller
# then sets `row.lower_bound = true`, where the typed run adds the declared
# callback row and leaves the bound clear. An exported row with `lower_bound`
# merges into the importer as the top row (`mergeImportedEffect`). The untyped
# result is therefore never narrower than the typed result.
packages/tools/src/precompile_imports.zig analyzeImportedFunction catch-block
packages/tools/src/precompile_imports.zig analyzeImportedFunction catch-block@2
packages/tools/src/precompile_imports.zig analyzeImportedFunction catch-block@3

# `effects.analyze` and `exportEffects` run after the flow target is set. A
# failure, including OutOfMemory, returns the result with its default effect
# `.blocked`, which merges into the importer as the top row. The flow target
# does not depend on the effect result, and the effect side stays blocked.
packages/tools/src/precompile_imports.zig analyzeImportedFunction catch-return
packages/tools/src/precompile_imports.zig analyzeImportedFunction catch-return@2

# The gate attributes these two rows to the nested helper `at`, because the
# scanner keeps the last `fn` name it saw. Both sites belong to
# `scanImportedFileTree`. A file that fails to load or fails IR validation
# returns a blocked fault entry. `scanImportRecords` in path_generator.zig
# turns every entry except `.clean` into an unseen failable call, so a blocked
# import cannot read as scanned clean. OutOfMemory propagates at the second.
packages/tools/src/precompile_imports.zig at catch-return
packages/tools/src/precompile_imports.zig at catch-switch

# Zig 0.17 removes captured errdefer. The validation catch retains an OOM
# poison flag and returns the original error. The population catches preserve
# the former errdefer's retained failure and also return the original error;
# none can turn a failed analysis into a verdict.
packages/zts/src/type_env.zig populateSourceTypesImpl catch-block
packages/zts/src/type_env.zig populateSourceTypesImpl catch-block@2
packages/zts/src/type_env.zig populateParsedDeclaration catch-block

# BoolChecker records an allocation failure with markAllocationFailure, and
# `check` returns OutOfMemory when the flag is set. No caller reads a boolean
# verdict from a checker that took a failed allocation. The poison and block
# catches only defer that failure until `check` reports it.
packages/zts/src/bool_checker.zig addDiagnostic catch-block
packages/zts/src/bool_checker.zig annotateNodeType catch-poison
packages/zts/src/bool_checker.zig annotateNodeType catch-poison@2
packages/zts/src/bool_checker.zig installGuards catch-poison
packages/zts/src/bool_checker.zig resolveFacts catch-block
packages/zts/src/bool_checker.zig restoreGuards catch-poison
packages/zts/src/bool_checker.zig scanImports catch-poison
packages/zts/src/bool_checker.zig scanImports catch-poison@2
packages/zts/src/bool_checker.zig walkExpr catch-poison
packages/zts/src/bool_checker.zig walkStmt catch-poison
packages/zts/src/bool_checker.zig walkStmt catch-poison@2
packages/zts/src/bool_checker.zig walkStmt catch-poison@3
packages/zts/src/bool_checker.zig walkStmt catch-poison@4
packages/zts/src/bool_checker.zig walkStmt catch-poison@5

# A schema that fails to parse is classified `.breaking`, the most severe
# change. The catch can raise the classification of an upgrade and can never
# lower it to `.unchanged`.
packages/zts/src/contract_diff.zig compareSchemaJson catch-return
packages/zts/src/contract_diff.zig compareSchemaJson catch-return@2

# Each switch propagates OutOfMemory and maps every other parse failure to a
# named verdict: `unparsable` for `compare`, and false for
# `importsOnlyBuiltinModules`. Neither answer says two sources are identical or
# that the imports are all built in. `Parsed.init` maps every non-memory parser
# error to NoTree, which both callers turn into one of those two answers.
packages/zts/src/ir_identity.zig compare catch-switch
packages/zts/src/ir_identity.zig compare catch-switch@2
packages/zts/src/ir_identity.zig importsOnlyBuiltinModules catch-switch
packages/zts/src/ir_identity.zig init catch-switch

# A spent work budget leaves the match not provably exhaustive, or drops only
# the redundancy verdict. The first adds the ZTS205 warning and reports
# exhaustive only when the arms were proven to cover the type. The second drops
# the ZTS216 unreachable-arm warning, which no verdict depends on. OutOfMemory
# propagates in both. `renderTop` sets `open`, which renders the witness as
# `default`, the widest text; it changes no verdict.
packages/zts/src/match_analysis.zig analyze catch-switch
packages/zts/src/match_analysis.zig analyze catch-switch@2
packages/zts/src/match_analysis.zig renderTop catch-switch

# An allocation failure poisons the checker, and `ensureHealthy` fails the
# pipeline before the narrowed type of the arm is used. Null is the untyped
# placeholder while the poisoned checker unwinds.
packages/zts/src/type_checker.zig findUnionMemberForPattern catch-block

# StrictChecker records an allocation failure with markAllocationFailure, and
# `check` returns OutOfMemory when the flag is set. A failed diagnostic or
# table write therefore cannot reach a reported verdict. The block, poison, and
# multiline catches only defer that failure until `check` reports it.
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig addDiagnostic catch-block
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig addRawBoundaryDiagnostic catch-block
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig addRawBoundaryDiagnostic catch-block@2
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig checkAmbientGlobal catch-block
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig checkAmbientGlobal catch-block@2
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig collectAnnotatedFunctions catch-poison
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig collectAnnotatedFunctions catch-poison@2
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig collectAnnotatedFunctions catch-poison@3
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig collectAnnotatedFunctions catch-poison@4
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig collectAssignments catch-multiline
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig collectAssignments catch-multiline@2
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig collectEntriesDerivedBindings catch-multiline
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig collectStaticLiterals catch-poison
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig countDeclaredName catch-block
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig recordCall catch-block
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig recordCall catch-block@2
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig resolveFacts catch-block
packages/zts/src/strict_checker.zig scanImports catch-poison
